#. help.theme
msgctxt "help.theme"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor theme <command>\n"
"\n"
"  list [--json]             installed themes\n"
"  current                   active theme\n"
"  apply <name>              apply a theme\n"
"  undo                      go back to the previous theme\n"
"  install <path> [--force]  install from a folder or .tar.gz\n"
"  export <name>             pack a theme into <name>.maxortheme\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor theme apply maxor-dark\n"
"    maxor theme undo\n"
"    maxor theme list --json"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor theme <comando>\n"
"\n"
"  list [--json]             temas instalados\n"
"  current                   tema activo\n"
"  apply <nombre>            aplica un tema\n"
"  undo                      vuelve al tema anterior\n"
"  install <ruta> [--force]  instala desde una carpeta o un .tar.gz\n"
"  export <nombre>           empaqueta un tema en <nombre>.maxortheme\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor theme apply maxor-dark\n"
"    maxor theme undo\n"
"    maxor theme list --json"

#. help.search
msgctxt "help.search"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor search [text] [--json] [--list]\n"
"\n"
"  In a terminal, with the full-screen app installed, it opens the Store\n"
"  (mark apps, install them, see details). With --list, --json or without\n"
"  a terminal it prints the results as a list.\n"
"\n"
"  --json    print JSON and nothing else\n"
"  --list    print the list instead of opening the Store\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor search brave\n"
"    maxor search --list firefox"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor search [texto] [--json] [--list]\n"
"\n"
"  En una terminal, con la app de pantalla completa instalada, abre la Tienda\n"
"  (marca apps, instálalas, mira los detalles). Con --list, --json o sin\n"
"  terminal imprime los resultados como lista.\n"
"\n"
"  --json    imprime JSON y nada más\n"
"  --list    imprime la lista en vez de abrir la Tienda\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor search brave\n"
"    maxor search --list firefox"

#. help.install
msgctxt "help.install"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor install <app...> [--nix|--flatpak] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Installs without sudo or rebuild. An id with dots (org.mozilla.firefox)\n"
"  is Flatpak; any other name is nixpkgs. Force the source with the flags.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor install btop\n"
"    maxor install org.mozilla.firefox\n"
"    maxor install --nix vlc"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor install <app...> [--nix|--flatpak] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Instala sin sudo ni reconstruir. Un id con puntos (org.mozilla.firefox)\n"
"  es Flatpak; cualquier otro nombre es nixpkgs. Fuerza el origen con las opciones.\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor install btop\n"
"    maxor install org.mozilla.firefox\n"
"    maxor install --nix vlc"

#. help.remove
msgctxt "help.remove"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor remove <app...> [--purge] [--list-data] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Removes apps installed with maxor. Folders the app left in your home\n"
"  (named exactly like the app) are listed; --purge deletes them too, and\n"
"  also cleans up after an app that is already gone. --list-data only lists them.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor remove btop\n"
"    maxor remove atlauncher --purge"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor remove <app...> [--purge] [--list-data] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Quita apps instaladas con maxor. Las carpetas que la app dejó en tu carpeta\n"
"  personal (con el mismo nombre que la app) se listan; --purge las borra también,\n"
"  y además limpia lo que dejó una app que ya no está. --list-data solo las lista.\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor remove btop\n"
"    maxor remove atlauncher --purge"

#. help.apps
msgctxt "help.apps"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor apps [list [--json] | updates | update [app...] | open <app> | repair]\n"
"\n"
"  list      installed apps (default)\n"
"  updates   apps that have a newer version (--refresh to look again, --notify to tell you)\n"
"  update    update every app, or just the ones you name\n"
"  open      open an installed app\n"
"  repair    show Flatpak apps in the app menu and the terminal\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor apps\n"
"    maxor apps updates\n"
"    maxor apps update btop\n"
"    maxor apps open brave"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor apps [list [--json] | updates | update [app...] | open <app> | repair]\n"
"\n"
"  list      apps instaladas (por defecto)\n"
"  updates   apps con una versión más nueva (--refresh para volver a mirar, --notify para avisarte)\n"
"  update    actualiza todas las apps, o solo las que nombres\n"
"  open      abre una app instalada\n"
"  repair    muestra las apps Flatpak en el menú de apps y en la terminal\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor apps\n"
"    maxor apps updates\n"
"    maxor apps update btop\n"
"    maxor apps open brave"

#. help.update
msgctxt "help.update"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor update [-y] [--no-lock] [--check] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Updates the flake inputs, builds the system without applying it, shows\n"
"  what changes and asks before switching.\n"
"\n"
"  -y, --yes   apply without asking\n"
"  --no-lock   do not update flake.lock\n"
"  --check     stop after showing the changes\n"
"  --json      same check, as JSON and nothing else (implies --check)\n"
"  --status    JSON: branch of the configuration, nixpkgs channel and generation (instant)\n"
"  --cached    JSON: the last saved check, or null\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor update\n"
"    maxor update --no-lock -y"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor update [-y] [--no-lock] [--check] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Actualiza las entradas del flake, construye el sistema sin aplicarlo, muestra\n"
"  qué cambia y pregunta antes de cambiar.\n"
"\n"
"  -y, --yes   aplica sin preguntar\n"
"  --no-lock   no actualiza flake.lock\n"
"  --check     se detiene después de mostrar los cambios\n"
"  --json      la misma comprobación, en JSON y nada más (implica --check)\n"
"  --status    JSON: rama de la configuración, canal de nixpkgs y generación (al instante)\n"
"  --cached    JSON: la última comprobación guardada, o null\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor update\n"
"    maxor update --no-lock -y"

#. help.rollback
msgctxt "help.rollback"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor rollback [N] [-y] | --list [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Goes back to the previous generation, or to generation N.\n"
"  --list shows the latest generations (--json for programs).\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor rollback --list\n"
"    maxor rollback 33"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor rollback [N] [-y] | --list [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Vuelve a la generación anterior, o a la generación N.\n"
"  --list muestra las últimas generaciones (--json para programas).\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor rollback --list\n"
"    maxor rollback 33"

#. help.doctor
msgctxt "help.doctor"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor doctor\n"
"\n"
"  Checks system, session, graphics, boot, identity and configuration.\n"
"  Exit code 1 if something is wrong.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor doctor\n"
"    maxor doctor --json | jq .groups"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor doctor\n"
"\n"
"  Comprueba sistema, sesión, gráficos, arranque, identidad y configuración.\n"
"  Código de salida 1 si algo va mal.\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor doctor\n"
"    maxor doctor --json | jq .groups"

#. help.hardware
msgctxt "help.hardware"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor hardware [show | detect [--write [path]]]\n"
"\n"
"  show      detected machine and the drivers Maxor uses (default)\n"
"  detect    print hardware.json; --write saves it for this machine\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor hardware\n"
"    maxor hardware detect --write"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor hardware [show | detect [--write [ruta]]]\n"
"\n"
"  show      el equipo detectado y los controladores que usa Maxor (por defecto)\n"
"  detect    imprime hardware.json; --write lo guarda para este equipo\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor hardware\n"
"    maxor hardware detect --write"

#. help.profile
msgctxt "help.profile"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor profile [list [--json] | enable <name> [-y|--no-apply] | disable <name> [-y|--no-apply]]\n"
"\n"
"  Profiles: gaming, dev, creator, office.\n"
"  --no-apply   only save the choice; apply it later with maxor update\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor profile enable gaming\n"
"    maxor profile disable dev --no-apply"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor profile [list [--json] | enable <nombre> [-y|--no-apply] | disable <nombre> [-y|--no-apply]]\n"
"\n"
"  Perfiles: gaming, dev, creator, office.\n"
"  --no-apply   solo guarda la elección; aplícala después con maxor update\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor profile enable gaming\n"
"    maxor profile disable dev --no-apply"

#. help.ui
msgctxt "help.ui"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor ui [home|store|themes|update|doctor|profiles]\n"
"\n"
"  Opens the full-screen app on that screen (home by default).\n"
"  It takes over your terminal and gives it back, with a short summary,\n"
"  when you quit. Running maxor with no arguments does the same.\n"
"  MAXOR_NO_TUI=1 disables that.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor\n"
"    maxor ui store"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor ui [home|store|themes|update|doctor|profiles]\n"
"\n"
"  Abre la app de pantalla completa en esa pantalla (home por defecto).\n"
"  Toma tu terminal y te la devuelve, con un resumen corto, cuando sales.\n"
"  Ejecutar maxor sin argumentos hace lo mismo. MAXOR_NO_TUI=1 lo desactiva.\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor\n"
"    maxor ui store"

#. help.setup
msgctxt "help.setup"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor setup\n"
"\n"
"  Opens the setup assistant: pick a look, choose profiles and review\n"
"  what was detected. Safe to run again any time.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor setup"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor setup\n"
"\n"
"  Abre el asistente de configuración: elige un aspecto, elige perfiles y revisa\n"
"  lo que se detectó. Se puede ejecutar de nuevo cuando quieras.\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor setup"

#. help.backup
msgctxt "help.backup"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor backup [file] [--json] | --list <file>\n"
"\n"
"  Saves what is yours in one .tar.gz: the active profiles, your own themes,\n"
"  the DankMaterialShell settings and the list of installed apps.\n"
"  hardware.json is not included: each computer detects its own.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor backup\n"
"    maxor backup ~/Documents\n"
"    maxor backup --list copia.tar.gz"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor backup [archivo] [--json] | --list <archivo>\n"
"\n"
"  Guarda lo tuyo en un .tar.gz: los perfiles activos, tus propios temas,\n"
"  los ajustes de DankMaterialShell y la lista de apps instaladas.\n"
"  hardware.json no se incluye: cada equipo detecta el suyo.\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor backup\n"
"    maxor backup ~/Documents\n"
"    maxor backup --list copia.tar.gz"

#. help.restore
msgctxt "help.restore"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor restore <file> [--apps] [-y]\n"
"\n"
"  Brings a backup back: profiles, themes, shell settings and the theme in use.\n"
"  --apps also installs the apps in the backup. Nothing existing is overwritten\n"
"  except the shell settings (a copy is kept next to them).\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor restore copia.tar.gz\n"
"    maxor restore copia.tar.gz --apps -y"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor restore <archivo> [--apps] [-y]\n"
"\n"
"  Recupera una copia: perfiles, temas, ajustes del shell y el tema en uso.\n"
"  --apps también instala las apps de la copia. No se sobrescribe nada de lo que\n"
"  existe salvo los ajustes del shell (se guarda una copia a su lado).\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor restore copia.tar.gz\n"
"    maxor restore copia.tar.gz --apps -y"

#. help.logs
msgctxt "help.logs"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor logs [--last | --path]\n"
"\n"
"  (none)    last 40 lines of the log\n"
"  --last    details of the last failure\n"
"  --path    path of the log file\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor logs --last"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor logs [--last | --path]\n"
"\n"
"  (nada)    últimas 40 líneas del registro\n"
"  --last    detalles del último fallo\n"
"  --path    ruta del archivo de registro\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor logs --last"

#. help.debug
msgctxt "help.debug"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor debug\n"
"\n"
"  Writes maxor-debug-<date>.txt here with version, hardware, doctor and log.\n"
"  Review it before sharing.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor debug"
msgstr ""
"Uso: maxor debug\n"
"\n"
"  Escribe aquí maxor-debug-<fecha>.txt con versión, hardware, doctor y registro.\n"
"  Revísalo antes de compartirlo.\n"
"\n"
"  Ejemplos:\n"
"    maxor debug"

